Cassian (Horus Heresy).wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Cassian''' was an [[Ultramarines]] [[Veteran Sergeant]] in the [[22nd Chapter (Ultramarines Legion)|22nd Chapter]], who took part in the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Calth]]'s [[Underground War]], during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
After the [[Word Bearers]] had corrupted [[Calth]]'s sun, [[Veridia]], into giving off deadly radiation, the [[Ultramarines]] trapped on on the world sought refuge beneath its surface. [[Consul-Chaplain]] [[Ankarion]] successfully led the remnants of the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s [[Space Marine Company|547th Company]] to the '''Auroran arcology''', which also sheltered two hundred thousand of Calth's population. The Company then sent a request for immediate aid, but due to the incursions by the World Bearers, who also sought to escape Veridian's radiation, the Ultramarines' central command on Calth lost contact with Auroran. As their request bore the Legion's highest priority, Thesian was sent to investigate what had happened to the archeology. Commanding the [[22nd Chapter (Ultramarines Legion)|22nd Chapter]]'s [[Destroyer Marine|4th Destroyer]] [[Space Marine Company|Company]], he entered Ankarion and his forces were quickly attacked by the Word Bearers and the 547th's [[Possession|animated]] corpses. Cassian served in the 4th Destroyer Company during this battle and was among its forces that succeeded in fighting their way to the former headquarters of the 547th. When they reached it, however, they discovered it had been turned into a fane to the [[Chaos God]] [[Nurgle]]. They also found Ankarion there, but he stood beside a group of Word Bearers and [[Chaos]] icons. The Consul-Chaplain now wore a suit of crimson [[power armor]], though, and his helmet was an indistinguishable mass of eyes, fanged mouths and curving horns. As Cassian and the 4th Destroyer Company realized Ankarion had betrayed the [[Ultramarines]], the corrupted [[Chaplain]] bellowed a challenge in ancient [[Colchis|Colchisian]] and charged at them. The Word Bearers and the animated corpses of the 547th followed him, along with [[Daemon]]s made from shadows.{{Fn|1}} 

However the [[Destroyer Marine|4th Destroyer]] [[Space Marine Company|Company]] charged at Ankarion's forces as well, as they had become enraged that a fellow [[Ultramarine]] was responsible for the '''Auroran arcology''''s corruption. [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Valius Thesian]] and Ankarion then dueled each other, but the fallen [[Chaplain]] fatally wounded Thesian with an obsidian spear. With the last of his strength, though, the Captain activated a [[melta bomb]], which consumed both him and Ankarion. The fighting between their surviving forces continued, but the [[Ultramarine]] [[Contemptor Dreadnought]] [[Andronicus (Dreadnought)|Andronicus]] began a wild rampage after his fellow Contemptor [[Dorian (Dreadnought)|Dorian]] was killed during the battle. The enraged Andronicus tore apart multiple foes and also destroyed a [[Chaos]] icon within the fane. Its destruction, though, put an end to the 547th's [[Possession|animated]] corpses and allowed the 4th Destroyer Company to defeat the remaining Word Bearers. Cassian would then take command of the survivors and they would report what had occurred to the arcology. This later led the Ultramarines' central command to destroy Auroran with [[atomic bomb]]s.{{Fn|1}}

