'''Castor''' is a [[Cadia]]n [[Lord General]] who led elements of the [[Cadian 8th]]{{Fn|1b}} as well as several other [[Cadian Regiment]]s sent to [[Subsector Aurelia|Sub Sector Aurelia]] to restore order.{{Fn|1c}}

==Biography==
===Before the Third Aurelian Crusade===
[[Lord General]] Castor had led his men for a century{{Fn|1b}} and is known to have personally hunted down and slain special beasts for his trophy collection.{{Fn|1d}}

When the [[Blood Ravens]]' civil war erupted and the subsector was plunged into another disaster, he was called upon by the Loyalists in the subsector and he brought with him the [[Cadian 8th]] [[Regiment]] that he personally led along with several [[Cadian Shock Troops]] Regiments to restore order in the subsector.{{Fn|1e}}

===Third Aurelian Crusade===
Ten years after the events of the [[Second Aurelian Crusade]] [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]] accompanied [[Lord General]] Castor and his men in hunting down a [[Hive Lord]]. Their hunting party was ambushed with only Castor, Adrastia and a single [[Guardsman]] who ran off and charged the [[Tyranid]]s ahead of them. Castor and Adrastia quickly hunted down and rescued the man before the [[Tyranid]]s could kill him. [[Imperial_Guard_Hierarchy|Sergeant-Major]] [[Merrick]] healed himself up and was introduced to Inquisitor Adrastia, then the group continued on to hunt down the Hive Lord. Along the way they encountered an [[Astra Militarum]] outpost and requested several squads of [[Cadian Shock Troopers]] to bolster their army and fought the Tyranids lying in ambush. Eventually the Lord General and his men found the Hive Lord's location and killed it. After the death of the Hive Lord, they regrouped with [[Commissar Lord]] [[Bernn]] and Inquisitor Adrastia revealed her true agenda to the [[Cadian 8th]] about the impending [[Exterminatus]] Fleet.{{Fn|1d}}{{Fn|1f}}

With this revelation Castor agreed to help Adrastia; she would accompany Castor, Merrick and Bernn in finding evidence to save the sector. The Inquisitor suggested finding [[teleportarium]]s in order to keep their movements hidden from '''High Command'''; one of said teleportariums was located within traitor heretical territory.{{Fn|1f}}

Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted a [[vox]] transmission from the [[Commander]] of the [[Cadian 39th (Traitor Guard)|Cadian 39th]], who openly declared mutiny against Imperial High Command and gunned down anyone who entered their territory. Castor decided to enter the territory and find the Teleportarium. During the mission they were hunted by the Cadian 39th's Traitor Commander, who fielded a [[Baneblade]] against them. Lord General Castor and his men pushed through Traitor outposts and [[Alpha Legion]] reinforcements hunting them down. The group was eventually cornered when the Traitor Commander blocked their path with his Baneblade and several turrets. Castor improvised and destroyed the turrets' targeting [[cogitator]] which turned on the Traitor's Baneblade and destroyed him. They found the teleportarium and moved onto their next objective within the hour.{{Fn|1g}}      

====Calderis====
While scouting for clues on [[Calderis]], Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted vox transmissions from Traitor [[Blood Ravens]] with disturbing a mission about destroying '''Argus Settlement''' and any evidence of the "Ascendant". Castor decided to save the settlement and openly fought the Traitor [[Blood Ravens]] to prevent a slaughter. The group managed to save important infrastructure from destruction and counterattacked against the Blood Ravens. Despite heavy casualties, Castor and the [[Cadian 8th]] destroyed the Traitors' Headquarters and killed [[Sergeant]] [[Lysandros]].{{Fn|1h}}

After the deaths of the Traitor Blood Ravens, Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted vox transmissions regarding an [[Ork]] [[Waaagh!|Waagghhhh]] led by a [[Warboss]] named [[Smashface]] moving their looted gear. The group deployed near the convoy and gathered as many resources as they could in order to fight back against the Orks in order to prevent the Waagghhhh from getting stronger. Lord General Castor and his men arrived just in time to the captured supply depot, killed the remaining ork defenders, destroyed several bridges to lure the Orks' convoy into killzones and then he called in additional reinforcements strong enough to eradicate the convoy. Eventually Castor and his men destroyed the convoy and prevented the Waagghhhh from growing.{{Fn|1i}}

====Aurelia====
After securing the [[teleportarium]] on [[Calderis]] the group went to [[Aurelia]] to stop elements of the [[Alpha Legion]] after Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted their vox transmissions regarding rebuilding a [[Dark Portal]] to summon [[Daemon]]s onto Aurelia again. Early on the mission [[Lord General]] Castor and his men captured the teleportarium but couldn't use it due to the influence of the Dark Portal. The group changed their objective and set about destroying the portal itself before Daemons and Alpha Legion reinforcements would overwhelm Aurelia. Unleashing the full might of the [[Cadian 8th]], Castor and his men destroyed the Dark Portal and slaughtered the remaining survivors.{{Fn|1j}}

On [[Aurelia]] Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted additional vox transmissions from the [[31st Harakoni Warhawks]] corrupted by [[Ulkair]], who had taken over a munitions dump. Castor decided that the group must kill the Warhawks' Commander and secure the munition dump. Along the way, Castor and his men were bombarded by batteries of [[Manticore]]s, but despite the artillery strikes they still pushed through and destroyed Traitor units before regrouping with Loyalist elements of the 31st Harakoni. The group arrived at the munitions dump, found the last remaining Loyalist officer of the 31st and agreed to help him and his men secure the munitions dump from the Traitors. The munitions dump was secured with the Harakoni officer thanking the Lord General and his men for saving them. When the battle was over Castor gave the Commander an official commendation. With the munitions dump secured, the group headed out to find and kill the Traitor Harakoni Commander. Despite the heavy casualties Castor and his men prevailed in not only killing the Commander but also destroying the Manticore batteries and crippling or destroying the majority of the Traitor Harakoni.{{Fn|1k}}

With [[Aurelia]] secured, [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]] decided that the group should head out towards [[Meridian]] and she pinpointed a potential location of the '''Lord Ascendant''' would send a personal transmission to Renegades and Traitors. She had full confidence in the Lord General's ability to destroy the Traitor regiments and was eager to find out the Lord Ascendant.{{Fn|1f}}

====Meridian====
While on [[Meridian]] [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]] intercepted a vox transmission of the Traitor [[Cadian 110th]] as they reported the successful coup attempt and slaughtered every Loyalist on '''Capitol Spire''' and waiting additional orders from the '''Lord Ascendant'''. The group deployed near a [[Astra Militarum]] base captured by the [[Cadian 110th]] and after intense fighting managed to recapture it and use it as a staging ground but not before one of the [[Leman Russ Battle Tank|Leman Russ tanks]] retreated and the Cadian 110th [[Sergeant]] ordered an assault line of [[Bane Wolf]]s on their position. Castor and his men succeed in pushing back the counterattack but the situation got worse when they intercepted vox transmissions indicating the Cadian 110th had established an air command bunker calling in airstrikes on Loyalist positions. Castor and his men marched on and destroyed Traitor units along the way despite being bombarded by airstrikes. Eventually the air command bunker was destroyed and the group proceeded to head out and destroy the Cadian 110th's headquarters. Castor and his men succeeded in destroying the HQ but not before they intercepted the Lord Ascendant's orders.{{Fn|1l}}

With the Capitol Spire secured from the traitors, Sergeant-Major Merrick intercepted [[Ork]] vox transmissions within [[Meridian]] and suggested to Lord General Castor that they should capture or gather resources from the Orks and investigate a potential hidden weapon made by the Orks named '''Daisy'''. After arriving in the sector, Castor immediately ordered his men to move and secure the power nodes to prevent the Orks from using them to power up Daisy. After destroying several Ork outposts and securing all 3 power nodes, the [[Nob|Ork Nob]] leading the clan revealed the secret weapon and fought the Lord General and his weapon on a [[Battle Wagon]]. After intense fighting Castor and his men prevailed and killed the Orks.{{Fn|1m}}

[[Meridian]] finally secured, Inquisitor Adrastia determined the source of the transmission was on [[Typhon Primaris]] but she still could not confirm if the Lord Ascendant was [[Chapter Master]] [[Azariah Kyras]]. A heated debate transpired when Merrick frustrated with the [[Inquisitor]] not outright calling him a Traitor and a Heretic. Castor managed to calm everyone down and continued their investigation and save the sector from the [[Exterminatus]] Fleet.{{Fn|1f}}

====Typhon Primaris====
Arriving on [[Typhon Primaris]] the group was ambushed by an [[Aeldari]] Warhost with a [[Warp Spider]] [[Exarch]] protecting the [[Seer Council]] and send in his own troops against Lord General Castor and his men. The ambush was a failure and Castor decided to destroy the Aeldari warhost permanently on Typhon Primaris. The group continued pursuing the Aeldari and destroyed a [[Webway Gate]] to prevent reinforcements from overwhelming them. Despite the Warp Spider Exarch teleporting the Seer Council to safety every time they were discovered by Castor and his men, eventually they all died from the pursuit but not before the Exarch cursed their pursuers about the impending doom on the Subsector.{{Fn|1n}}  

While continuing their investigation on Typhon Primaris, Adrastia, Castor, Merrick and Bernn were contacted by [[Chapter Master]] [[Azariah Kyras]]; he revealed to them that the Aeldari Warhost prevented him from guiding the [[Exterminatus]] Fleet from arriving in the sector. With the Seer Council dead nothing would prevent the destruction of Typhon Primaris as the Fleet readying their payloads and started an [[Orbital Bombardment]]. Castor started to panic and rushed his men to safety to the best of his ability while being mocked by Kyras. Despite being bombarded by the Exterminatus Fleet, the Lord General and his men managed to arrive in an arena and had no choice but to accept a challenge from a [[Alpha Legion]] [[Chaos Champion]] in order to escape. The Champion was defeated and the Lord General and his men escaped Typhon Primaris before the planet died.{{Fn|1o}}  

====Judgement of Carrion====
After using the [[teleportarium]] to escape the Exterminatus of Typhon Primaris, the survivors arrived on the ''[[Judgement of Carrion]]''. Merrick snapped and attempted to shoot Castor due to him losing his men on Typhon Primaris and watching them die. Castor calmed the Sergeant-Major and revealed to him and Adrastia the actual location of [[Azariah Kyras]] after piecing the clues together. With the knowledge he provided, The Lord General convinced everyone to find a way to escape and stop Kyras on [[Cyrene]]. While trying to find a way to escape the ''Judgement of Carrion''', An [[Ork]] Mad [[Mek]] announced them as trespassers and sent his own troops against the Lord General. Castor rallied his troops and attacked the Ork camps and destroyed them to prevent reinforcements arriving on the ''Judgement of Carrion''. Eventually the Lord General and his men prevailed; with the Mek dead and his clan destroyed, the ''Judgement of Carrion'' was secured.{{Fn|1p}}

While inside the ''Judgement of Carrion'', Merrick found interesting logs and reported his findings to the Lord General regarding precious cargo hidden away inside the ''Judgement'' and suggested securing it for the [[Cadian 8th]]. Castor agreed and protected the labour engine and its cargo hold from the [[Tyranid]]s. The mission was a success and its cargo would be used against [[Azariah Kyras]].{{Fn|1q}} 

====Cyrene====
Before confronting Kyras, Merrick intercepted vox communications on [[Cyrene]] regarding the [[Alpha Legion]] [[Warband]], Traitor [[Blood Ravens]] and '''Cadian 85th Fire Drakes''' scavenging weapons and vehicles such as a [[Land Raider]] to be used for Kyras' army. Arriving on Cyrene to investigate the Traitor's plans, Castor and Merrick spotted a [[Baneblade]] tank and quickly captured it and used it against the Traitors and Heretics. With the help of the Baneblade, Castor ordered a full assault on the headquarters of all three armies to weaken Kyras and prevent additional reinforcements from sending aid to the [[Chapter Master]]. Despite the destruction of all three Headquarters, the Traitors and Heretics persisted and continued fighting due to the leadership of a [[Blood Ravens]] officer. The Blood Ravens officer rode on a [[Land Raider Redeemer]] fuelled by the powers of [[Chaos]] and desperately confronted the Lord General and his men. The final battle ended with the death of the Blood Ravens officer and the rest of the Traitors and Heretics routed.{{Fn|1r}}

With the amount of deaths happening in [[Subsector Aurelia]] due to the constant warfare and the [[Exterminatus]] of [[Typhon Primaris]], [[Azariah Kyras]] finally and slowly ascended into a [[Daemon Prince]] within the '''Pit of the Maledictus''' on [[Cyrene]]. [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Gabriel Angelos]],[[Librarian]] [[Jonah Orion]] and [[Blood Ravens]] Loyalists arrived early followed by [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]], Lord General Castor, Sergeant-Major Merrick, Lord Commissar Bernn and other members of the Cadian 8th. Angelos and his men went on ahead and battled their way against the [[Alpha Legion]] warband to confront Kyras. Meanwhile the Lord General and his men battled their way against a large concentration of the Alpha Legion, slowing them down. Angelos, Orion and the Loyalist Blood Ravens finally confronted Kyras and they tried to kill him before he fully ascended. During the battle Kyras ordered his troops to protect the Skull Towers as they provided him invulnerability against any attacks. Lord General Castor, upon hearing it on intercepted Alpha Legion vox communications immediately ordered his men to hunt down and destroy the Skull Towers in order to weaken Kyras. Despite destroying the first Skull Tower, Kyras critically wounded Angelos and killed Orion and the rest of the Blood Ravens who accompanied him. [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]], angered to see her old friend Angelos harmed, cursed Kyras and pledged to slay him herself. The battle continued with the Lord General and his men destroying several more Skull Towers and killing as many Alpha Legion [[Chaos Space Marines]] and [[Daemons]] who dared to slow them down. The final confrontation ended with Kyras killed by Castor after he called in an [[Orbital Bombardment]] on Kyras' location.{{Fn|1s}} 

The [[Exterminatus]] Fleet was called off due to [[Inquisitor]] [[Adrastia]] showing proof of [[Azariah Kyras|Kyras]]' death; she briefly said her goodbyes to Castor and Merrick then left the [[Sub-sector]] after her investigation. Despite Merrick's attempt to murder his superior officer, Castor gave him a medal and did nothing to punish him.{{Fn|1t}}

