Chettamandey Vula Brobantis.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Chettamandey Vula Brobantis''', informally called '''Chetta Brobantis''', is the current [[Novator]] of the [[Navigator]] [[House Brobantis]], though she was not born of the House.{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Chettamandey Vula was born to the [[Navis Nobilite]] [[House Dacastos]] and married off to House Brobantis to shore up the ailing fortunes of House Dacastos. {{Fn|2a}} At some point in Chetta's past, she used to fly with the [[19th Pacificum]] [[battlefleet]].{{Fn|2b}}

===Necromunda===
{{Spoiler|source=A Common Ground (Short Story)}}
She had instead taken the position from her husband, [[Azariel Brobantis]], after he was killed by the [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]] [[House Goliath]] [[Pit Fighters|pit fighter]] [[Jaxx]], while they watched a fight in one of [[Hive Primus]]' arenas. What no ones knows however, is that Chettamandey had secretly met with Jaxx beforehand, and had persuaded him to kill her husband. This had been after Jaxx was being medically healed, because he disobeyed the arena's '''impresario''', '''Drost Khouren''''s, order to lose in the fight Chettamandey and her husband had been watching. To guarantee he lost, Drost had spiked Jaxx's [[combat drug|stimms]] before the match and the injured pit fighter was now disillusioned and angered that he was being prevented from earning more fame and money to take care of his family. It was at moment that Chettamandey appeared and made her offer that the pit fighter kill her husband, in Jaxx's next match, while making it look like Drost was his true target. Though he was reluctant at first, especially after she promised he would be painlessly killed afterwards, Chettamandey swore that if Jaxx agreed, she would use her vast wealth to ensure the pit fighter's family was well taken care of. After hearing this Jaxx agreed, as it would allow him to get revenge on Drost, but more importantly it would guarantee his family's future and that the pit fighter's name would be remembered.{{Fn|1}} 

After their successful agreement, Chettamandey then returned to her husband, Azariel and acted like nothing was remiss. Though she had never loved him, the two were close partners in their arraigned marriage, until Azariel had begun ignoring her warnings and concerns, when it came to managing House Brobantis' affairs. The final line was crossed, though, after Azariel had completed arraigned marriages for their two children, [[Felicia Brobantis]] and [[Ranovel Brobantis]], based on what would best help their House. Chettamandey was vehemently against Azariel's plans, as she did not want the children's marriages to be political arrangements like theirs was, but her pleas were dismissed, as it was Azariel's right as Novator to do so. This immediately caused Chettamnadey to begin looking for ways to kill Azariel, without anyone finding out she was responsible. The chance finally came, when they traveled to Necromunda and their host '''Adelard''' [[House Ko'iron|Ko'iron]] took them to see several of impresario Drost Khouren's fights. Now when Jaxx's next match began, Chettamnadey simply watched as the pit fighter jumped into their stand and swung a cleaver at Drost. Just as they had arraigned however, Jaxx intentionally missed at the last second and instead bisected Azariel, who had been sitting next to the impresario. As her husband fell dead in pieces, Chettamandey allowed Jaxx to kill Drost, before she then in turn killed the pit fighter with her [[Warp Eye]]. In the chaotic aftermath, Chettamandey quickly left Necromunda to take command of House Brobantis; but not before arranging to pay Jaxx's relatives a sizeable 10,000 credits, in the [[Hive World]]'s currency.{{Fn|1}}

===Vorlese===
{{Spoiler|source=Rites of Passage (Novel)}}
As Chetta was returning to [[Vorlese]] for her recently deceased husband's wake, she would come across a strange phenomenon after the Navigator currently on shift mysteriously died. She would guide the ship out of the Warp in the Gallimo System only to find that [[Gallimo Prime]] had disappeared. Using her third eye she traced the ripples in the warp to a small cut in real-space bleeding small amounts of warp energies. Realizing that entire planet was pulled into the warp in some deliberate manner, she would order that her ship leave an continue to Vorlese.{{Fn|2a}}

