Cluggan.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
[[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Sergeant]] '''Cluggan''' was one of the initial founding members of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[regiment]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

He is described as big and grey-haired. Cluggan was popular with the men, and considered dependable by [[Ibram Gaunt]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} He was also known to have been an amateur military historian.{{Fn|1c}}


==Biography==
On [[Blackshard]], Cluggan took part in the raid on a [[Chaos]] citadel and was in the vanguard with [[Colonel]] [[Colm Corbec|Corbec]].{{Fn|1a}}

On [[Voltemand]], Cluggan took part in the counter-ambush against the [[World Eater]] Traitor Marines who were threatening the [[Ketzok 17th Armoured Regiment]]. Colonel-Commissar [[Ibram Gaunt]] ordered Cluggan to take six men and scout out [[Pavis Crossroads]] to make sure it was in friendly hands. He completed this without incident.{{Fn|1b}}

During the assault on [[Voltis City]], Cluggan was given command of a considerable number of the Ghosts, to attack the secondary objective: the Western sanitation outfalls. After the assault on the primary objective failed, due to the cultists flooding the tunnels, Cluggan succeeded in his objective and blew away a hundred-meter section of the city's curtain wall. While making their way back through the [[Bokore Valley]], they were shelled by the [[Ketzok 17th Armoured Regiment]] under orders of [[General]] [[Noches Sturm]]. Cluggan died in the barrage.{{Fn|1b}}

