Colm Corbec.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source=Gaunt's Ghosts (Novel Series)}}
[[image:Colonel Colm Corbec.jpg|thumb|330px|right|Colm Corbec{{Fn|5}}]]
[[Colonel]] '''Colm Corbec''' was the second-in-command of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment]] from almost the inception of the regiment in 765.[[M41]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|3a}}


==Biography==
===Early Life===
Corbec was born to [[Landa Meroc]] on [[Tanith]]; since he was born out of wedlock, he ended up taking his father's name.{{Fn|3c}}

Corbec began his career as an apprentice to his father, who was a machine-smith and furniture-maker. After he grew too old to help his father, Corbec switched to working in the lumber-mills of [[Sottress]]. He worked there for a long time, eventually developing a lingering cough caused by the sawdust in the atmosphere. Corbec decided that a healthier job would be a good idea and joined the [[Tanith Magna]] [[PDF|Militia]].{{Fn|1b}}

===Sabbat Worlds Crusade===
Originally a standard [[Guardsman]], Colm Corbec was promoted directly to the rank of Colonel after the [[Fall of Tanith]] by [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]].{{Fn|3a}} Due to his promotion being seen as largely by chance, Corbec had to deal with some Tanith Guardsmen not treating him as an "actual" officer.{{Fn|2}}

He quickly formed a bond with Gaunt, and the two eventually became firm friends - Gaunt once in fact described him as a "brother" - although Corbec remained just as close to his comrades in the ranks, particularly [[Hlaine Larkin]], the famed [[Sniper]] (partly because they had both served in the Tanith Magna militia together){{Fn|2}}{{Fn|3a}} and [[Tolin Dorden]], regimental [[Medic|Chief Medical Officer]]. Corbec had actually been delivered by Dorden when the doctor was the County Pryze practitioner, and also felt that he owed Dorden his friendship due to the fact that Dorden saved the life of his mother, Landa.{{Fn|3c}} Despite initially entertaining doubts about his ability to command - particularly in his ability to issue orders that may have lead to the deaths of his soldiers - Corbec proved to be a charismatic, straight-talking and somewhat unconventional officer who appeared to be universally liked by his entire regiment, if not by everyone he happened to meet; Corbec and Colonel [[Gilbear]] of the [[Volpone Bluebloods]] came to serious blows on one occasion.{{Fn|3d}}
[[image:Corbec_inferno!030_2002_34.jpg|thumb|450px|right|Portrait of '''C. Corbec'''.]]
In the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]], Corbec was normally found leading the Ghost's 2nd Platoon{{Fn|3}}{{Fn|4}} but on occasions led the bulk of the entire regiment.{{Fn|1c}} This first occurred during the liberation of [[Caligula (Hive World)|Caligula]], where Corbec was forced to lead the majority of the Tanith regiment without the aid of Colonel-Commissar Gaunt, including devising a strategy to deal with a [[Daemon|daemonic entity]]. This experience finally gave Corbec the courage and self-belief to fully embrace the responsibilities of command.{{Fn|3b}} Later, on [[Menazoid Epsilon]], Gaunt left Corbec in charge while the Colonel-Commissar led a small insertion team to assist [[Fereyd|an Imperial intelligence officer]] in a secret mission to prevent a conspiracy taking control of the Crusade.{{Fn|1c}}

Corbec was a truly heroic man, who regularly appeared to perform feats of daring, recklessness, bravery and skill in combat. For example, he held the gate of the [[Nacedon]] field hospital by himself, armed with his [[lasgun|lasrifle]] and a [[flamer]], against hordes of [[Chaos Cults|cultists]]; he took a pig-tooth from the yard after this event to act as his lucky charm.{{Fn|3c}}

Badly wounded several times during his career, Colonel Corbec was shot dead by the traitorous Trooper [[Lijah Cuu]] while protecting the [[Saint Sabbat|Beati]] on Herodor. Out of respect for his close friend, Gaunt had Corbec buried in a coffin made completely out of [[nalwood]], a type of wood native to Tanith which is extremely rare after the planet's destruction.

==Appearance and Abilities==
Corbec was a big man, bigger than most Tanith, but not as tall as the notably lanky Ibram Gaunt. His size and bulk enabled him to have some success as a wrestler before joining the [[PDF|militia]]; he was Pryze County Champion three times running.{{Fn|3d}} He was pale, blue of eye and dark of hair, like most Tanith{{Fn|1a}} and always sported a bushy beard{{Fn|1a}} that was just slightly greater than regulation length.{{Cite this}} Gaunt in fact once despaired of his second's appearance, wondering how he was possibly going to enforce uniform discipline in the men when the colonel of the regiment looked like a "matted and tangled old man of the woods."{{Fn|2}}

His arms were thickly muscled, and tattooed with blue spirals.{{Fn|1a}} A regular smoker, showing a preference for liquorice-flavoured cigars after trying some given to him by a [[Basilisk]] commander from the [[Ketzok 17th Armoured|Ketzok ‘Serpents’]]{{Fn|3c}}, Corbec was missing the little finger from his left hand, which had been chopped off in combat. He preferred to sleep outside in the open air, if possible and had several hobbies, including wood-whittling and carving, bird watching and of course, drinking with his men.{{Cite this}}

Corbec wasn’t scared of much, but he did have a phobia about space-travel that lasted for several years. He carried bad memories of the time he was captured by [[Pater Sin]] and forced to watch the cruel murder of [[Trooper]] [[Yael (Tanith)|Yael]]; however, Colonel Corbec avenged Yael by killing Pater Sin on [[Herodor]].{{Cite this}}

