Corflich Loatheheart.wikitext:
{{TzeentchPortal}}
'''Corflich Loatheheart''' is a [[Daemon Prince]] of [[Tzeentch]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Corflich Loatheheart sought to gain power over the [[Murderval]], a warband of [[Chaos]] [[Daemon]]s, when its ruler [[Sssair Gleamling]] was defeated by [[Eldar]] and [[Dark Eldar]] upon the world of [[Lohiac]]. Loatheheart tricked Sssair into giving him control over the Muderval by promising that he would return it to him once it had claimed its millionth soul for Tzeentch. However, Sssair shortly found himself imprisoned within the [[Impossible Fortress]], and the Murderval fell fully under Loatheheart's rule.{{Fn|1}}

His first act was to eradicate the population of the [[Agri World]] [[Dortun]] in three nights of bloodshed and debauchery. Next he kidnapped three hundred [[Fire Warrior]]s from the [[Tau]] [[Sept]] world of [[Vior'la]] and deposited them within the [[Garden of Nurgle]] to be left to their own fates. Grandest of all his schemes was his vengeance upon the survivors of the battle of Lohiac. Loatheheart set a trap at the [[Death World]] of [[Raith]] by slaughtering its [[Imperial Guard]] garrison and waiting for a Dark Eldar raid to arrive. The Dark Eldar quickly sensed a trap and turned to depart but found their escape blocked by the Murderval. Scores of Dark Eldar were dragged screaming into the [[Warp]] and their [[Archon]] was run to ground and captured by Loatheheart within Raith's thick jungle. Loatheheart then proceeded to break both the Archon's arms and legs and gift her helpless body to [[Slaanesh]]'s [[Palace of Pleasure]] as a tribute from the new master of the Murderval.{{Fn|1}}

