Coron Grizmund.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
[[Image:Grizmund - Imperial Armour Volume One - Imperial Guard and Imperial Navy pg. 214.png|thumb|right|500px|Coron Grizmund on the Grace of the Throne, carrying the Narmenian Armoured [[Regimental Standard]]{{Fn|5}}]]
[[Lord General]] '''Coron Grizmund'''{{Fn|1c}} was the commanding officer of the [[Narmenian Armoured]] [[regiments]] taking part in the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]]. Holder of a distinguished reputation, Grizmund is best known for his actions during the [[Siege of Vervunhive]].

==Biography==
Reputed to be an excellent [[Tank Commander]], Grizmund first distinguished himself as [[Colonel]] of the [[1st Narmenian Armoured Regiment]] during the [[Cociaminus]] campaign of '''760-762.[[M41]]''', where his leadership was instrumental in the two major tank battles taking place on the dune sea outside the [[hive]] city of [[Harshen]], both of which were Imperial victories.{{Fn|2}}

In '''769.M41''' Grizmund, now a [[General]], led a unit of Narmenian Armour to the world of [[Verghast]], where he fought in the defence of [[Vervunhive]].{{Fn|1a}} During the Second Storm of the embattled [[Hive City]] he, along with his entire command staff, were arrested by the [[Vervunhive Primary Commissariat]], the local military police, for taking an unauthorized route to the battlefield, trying to circumvent a traffic jam caused by confused orders.{{Fn|1b}} While the situation looked grim for a while, [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]] eventually stepped in and had the charges dismissed; Grizmund was returned to his command.{{Fn|1c}}

The Narmenian Armoured regiment Grizmund led at Vervunhive was made up of 127 [[Leman Russ Battle Tank]]s, 27 [[Demolishers]], 42 [[Salamanders]] and a small number of [[Sentinel]] walkers and attached infantry, and with it General Grizmund managed to win considerable distinction in the campaign.{{Fn|1x}} In the counter attack from the stricken hive city Vervunhive, for example, have been destroyed 200 armoured vehicles just in one day of fighting. The men of general Grizmund refer to him as the 'fighting general' because he was not afraid to join the frontline with his men, and always willing to commit his troops to the heart of battle.{{Fn|5}}

Particularly of note was during "[[Operation Dercius]]", when a manoeuver Grizmund coined "The Scissors" was used to devastating effect. During this engagement the Naremenian Armour totally annihilated a much larger [[Zoican]] armoured force, losing only two tanks in the process. Grizmund was further able to mount a successful counterattack on Veyveyr Gate, driving the Zoican forces out from under the city's [[Void Shield]].{{Fn|1c}}

His personal tank was ''[[Grace of the Throne]]'' — special Leman Russ Battle Tank, where he would personally carry the [[regimental standard]].{{Fn|5}}

By 791.M41, he had been elevated to the position of [[Lord General]]. {{Fn|6}}

==[[Quotes Imperial Guard#G|Quotes]]==
*''"Target and deny! By our deaths shall they know us!"''{{Fn|1c}}
*''"Let's give them hell, men."''{{Fn|1c}}

