Cortamus.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Cortamus''' was a member of the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
He would be among the [[Imperial]] forces that were outside of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Eternity Gate (Imperial)|Eternity Gate]], when it was closed near the end of the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]]. Afterwards, Cortamus was among the [[Imperial]] forces that rallied under the leadership of the [[Imperial Fists]] Commander [[Archamus II]]{{Fn|1b}}. This allied force would fight many battles against the [[Traitor]] hordes, which included the defense of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s '''Delphine Viaduct'''{{Fn|1a}}. Cortamus would be among the Imperial Fists assigned to [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fafnir Rann]]{{Fn|1b}} and together with portions of the [[Blood Angels]] and [[White Scars]], they were sent to defend the causeway below the Viaduct.{{Fn|1a}} 

In the battle that followed, the [[Traitor]]s swarmed [[Fafnir Rann|Rann]]'s position and the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fisk Halen]] was nearly slain by the [[Word Bearer]] [[Sor Talgron]]. Rann intervened to save Fisk's life, but was then nearly overwhelmed by Talgron himself. This led Cortamus and the Imperial Fist [[Bedwyr]], to come to Rann's aid and the three then attacked the Word Bearer together. However Cortamus quickly died, due to either being too eager or too brave, while fighting Talgron and collapsed after the Imperial Fist's head was crushed into his body by the Word Bearer's [[Infernal Crozius]].{{Fn|1b}} 

