'''Corteswain''' was an [[Abbot]] of the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] who was later condemned for [[heresy]].

==History==
Engaged on the Mechanicus's never-ending quest to locate new [[Standard Template Construct]] systems, Corteswain travelled the [[galaxy]], examining archaeological sites.  One of these expeditions took Corteswain to an unnamed [[Dead World]], where his expedition was attacked, and only he survived.{{Fn|1a}}

When he returned to the [[Imperium]], Corteswain claimed to have been abducted and carried to a far-off planet by a being he described as a god.  In fact, he claimed to have seen the face of the [[Omnissiah]] itself.  He was condemned as a heretic by rival members of the Mechanicus, and expelled from the [[omniastery]] on [[Selethoth]] where he had been preaching.  He later disappeared and his fate is uncertain, though it is likely that his rivals had him abducted and killed in secret.{{Fn|1a}}

A portion of Corteswain's writings survived, describing the "god" he had seen and its wondrous space vessel.{{Fn|1a}}  These writings eventually came into the possession of the psychopathic industrialist [[Kasimir de Valtos]], who discovered the tomb of Corteswain's "god" on [[Pavonis]]: the [[Nightbringer]] and its space vessel, the ''[[Bringer of Darkness]]''.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

