==Etymology==
{{Trivia}}
*Corvus Corax is Latin for "Raven Heart".
*Corax's name comes from the Greek word ''Corax'', which means Raven and is also the species name for the [[Wikipedia:Common Raven|Common Raven]] (''Corvus corax'').
*Corax's last words are taken from the poem "[[Wikipedia: The Raven|The Raven]]" by [[Wikipedia:Edgar Allan Poe|Edgar Allan Poe]].

