{{IronHandsPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=Iron Hands member|OTHERUSE=Grey Knights Grand Master|OTHERPAGE=Crius (Grand Master)}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a member of the [[Iron Hands]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].

==Biography==
[[Image:Crius.jpeg|thumb|right|200px|Crius]]
Known as the Lord of [[Clan Kadoran]] and First Vexilla, {{PAGENAME}} was a member of the [[Crusader Host]] at the start of the Heresy. He was imprisoned along with the rest of the Crusader Host after the [[Battle of Isstvan III]]. However, he was freed by [[Rogal Dorn]] to hunt for [[Isstvan V]] survivors 214 days after word of [[Ferrus Manus]]'s death.{{Fn|1}}

Along with [[Boreas (Imperial Fists)|Boreas]], {{PAGENAME}} set out to find his lost Iron Hand brothers. Eventually, he and Boreas came across the ''[[Thetis]]'', an Iron Hand ship that was sending out a signal to lure enemy ships into a trap. However, {{PAGENAME}} and Boreas discovered that the Iron Hands were revenants that had been reanimated by the forbidden technologies of the [[Keys of Hel]].{{Fn|1}}

While the ''Thetis'' came under attack from [[Sons of Horus]], Boreas attempted to kill the revenants, but {{PAGENAME}} stopped him, becoming mortally wounded in the process. After being reanimated by the Keys of Hel, {{PAGENAME}} sent Boreas back to Terra in chains with a promise that if they were needed, they would answer. One word would be needed to summon them: Waken.{{Fn|1}}

