Cromwell.wikitext:
{{InquisitionPortal}}
'''Cromwell''' is a [[Radical]] [[Inquisitor]], who was declared a [[Traitor]] by the large [[Inquisition Conclave]] he served with, during the [[13th Black Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

His downfall began, when the [[Inquisition Conclave|Conclave]] was formed to investigate the [[Sentinel Worlds]], early in the [[13th Black Crusade|Crusade]]. This was after the region suffered strange power surges and an [[Emperor's Tarot]] reading foresaw dire omens there. Once they arrived, the Conclave's [[Inquisitors]] soon discovered that the forces of [[Chaos]] had activated an ancient [[Aeldari]] [[Warp Gate]]. Worse still, the Gate was being used to transport a powerful [[Daemon Prince]] into [[Realspace]]. This led the Conclave to do battle against the Chaos forces and both sides were also attacked by the Aeldari as well. However, the Conclave was not a united front in the battle and its different factions could not agree on a single course of action. As a result of this schism, Cromwell was declared a [[Traitor]] and the [[Puritan]] Inquisitor [[Allysa Collack]] entered the Warp Gate to stop the Daemon Prince from materializing. Though she was successful, Collack was declared lost afterwards. As for Cromwell, he was burned horribly by a flamer as the battle neared its end, but the Traitor survived and is now slowly regenerating.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
''Cromwell'' and [[Allysa Collack]] were created for the [[Inquisitor (Game)]] campaign, '''Shadows of Chaos'''.{{Fn|1}}
