Culcis.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Culcis''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Volpone 50th]] during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}


==Biography==
While still a [[Trooper]], Culcis was wounded in action on [[Nacedon]] and was left behind in a farmhouse being used as a field hospital when [[Imperial]] forces were forced to retreat from [[Lohenich]]. However, a unit of the [[Tanith First and Only]] discovered the wounded Volpone and their [[Chief Medical Officer]], [[Tolin Dorden]], refused to abandon men in need of medical assistance. The Tanith ended up leaving ten men behind to defend the farmstead and some of the less-injured Volpone, including Culcis, supported them. Together, they were able to survive the night against attacks by [[Chaos Cult]]ists until the Crusade forces pushed back and reclaimed the land that they had lost the previous day.{{Fn|1a}}

Culcis later distinguished himself on [[Vandamaar]], earning a medal for his valorous actions.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|2}} This, combined with favourable reports from both Dorden and his commander, [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]], resulted in Culcis being promoted to the Volpone 50th's elite Tenth Brigade. He later saw action as part of [[Inquisitor]] [[Lilith Abfequarn|Lilith's]] bodyguard detail on [[Monthax]].{{Fn|1b}}

By the time of the [[Siege of Vervunhive]], Culcis had been promoted to the rank of [[Major]]. There, he led a detachment of the Tenth Brigade defending the walls of [[Vervunhive]] during the first [[Ferrozoica|Zoican]] storm of the city. Culcis's force held the [[Sondar Gate]] against thousands of Zoican storm-troops, despite being reduced to hand-to-hand combat and suffering 70% losses; this included his immediate subordinate [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Mantes]], who sacrificed himself to blow up a Zoican siege engine. Culcis himself lost a hand in the fighting.{{Fn|2}}

