Cyan Angelus.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
'''Cyan Angelus''' was a [[Space Marine Commander|Commander]] in the [[Blood Angels]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was seasoned veteran of countless wars against the [[Asuryani]] and used his prowess and cunning in dispatching their [[Wraithlord]]s.{{Fn|1}} When the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]] began,{{Fn|2}} Angelus was among the [[Blood Angels]] who fought{{Fn|1}} the invading Asuryani in the [[Kith Campaign]].{{Fn|3}} The [[Space Marine Commander|Commander]] became a living legend for leading his [[Chapter]]'s [[1st Company (Blood Angels)|First Company]] deep into the territories held by the [[Craftworld]] [[Iyanden]]. During these battles, Angelus was able to destroy many of Craftworld's [[Ghost Warrior]]s, which were his most hated foes.{{Fn|1}} However the Commander's actions led to an awakening of an [[Avatar of Khaine]], who mocked Angelus by wearing the helm of a Ghost Warrior. Named the [[Avatar of the Bloody-Handed God]], the massive [[Xenos]] was able to take command of [[Iyanden]]'s failing fleets, as well as ghostly silent black armored Asuryani. It would then lead them against the Imperium and the order was given to spare no effort in destroying the Avatar's forces.{{Fn|4}} Angelus would take part in the effort, but was killed by the Asuryani.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Cyan Angelus'' and the [[Avatar of the Bloody-Handed God]] were created for the [[Dark Crusade Campaign]], by the '''Hobby Center''' staff of [[Games Workshop]]'s '''Harvard Square''' store{{Fn|1}} in '''Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA'''.{{Fn|3}}

