'''Cypher''' is a mysterious figure associated with the [[Dark Angels]]. Taking a pre-[[Horus Heresy|heresy]] title of office in [[The Order]], his role was that of keeper of secrets and traditions. The current Cypher is said to be one of [[The Fallen]].{{Fn|3}}

It is not even possible to deduce whether Cypher is for or against the [[Imperium]], an ally or enemy to those who betrayed the Dark Angels. Cypher does not always work alone, at times seeming to ally or associate himself with others. His presence upon a planet draws dangerous elements to him from across the galaxy. Whether this is through his bidding is unclear, but it is too recurrent to be mere happenstance. Ultimately, no matter if he is surrounded by others: Cypher is a loner, a rogue agent whose true intentions are unknown to those he has served alongside. Cypher’s targets and destinations are as inscrutable as everything else about him. Among his confirmed kills have been [[planetary governor]]s, [[Chaos Lord]]s, Space Marine [[Chapter Master]]s, [[Sorcerer|sorcerous covens]], [[cult]] leaders and high ranking [[Inquisitor]]s. He has fought alongside both [[Chaos Terminator]]s and [[Daemon Prince]]s as well as [[Imperial Guardsmen]] and [[Space Marine]]s. The one thing they all have in common is that they serve the purpose in his mysterious grand plan.{{Fn|5}}

==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Malediction (Audio Book)}}
[[Image:LordCypher.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The '''Lord Cypher''' during the [[Horus Heresy]]{{Fn|13}}]]
===Pre-Heresy===
'''Cypher''' itself was originally a title within [[the Order]] of [[Caliban]]. To ensure their proud traditions were maintained, the ruling Masters secretly selected a single member to become the Lord Cypher. Upon taking the title, the Lord Cypher renounced his own name, enshrouding his very appearance beneath cloak and hood. It was forbidden for any others to recognise his old self, for the Lord Cypher was to forsake his very personality, and from that day onwards was to instead embody the laws, customs and strict disciplines of the Order. He was tasked the responsibility of ensuring the traditions of the Order were upheld, and that the recruits and Masters alike were never allowed to degenerate from their lofty ideals. The Lord Cypher advised the Masters on all matters of protocol and officiated at many important ceremonies. The Lord Cypher was a lofty position, one which the Order took extremely seriously, for it was known that it was the nature of the galaxy to recede and structures to collapse. The Cypher that appears in the fortieth millennium embodies many of these ancient tenets, although there has never been any absolute connection.{{Fn|5}}

At least three Lord Cyphers have appeared in canon material:

*'''An elderly human Lord Cypher''', who advised [[Luther]] and [[Lion El’Jonson|the Lion]] during the campaign against the Great Beasts. He passed away before the coming of the [[Imperium]] to [[Caliban]].{{Fn|8}}
*'''A young Lord Cypher''', who was one of Luther's advisors during the first stages of his rebellion.{{Fn|1}} He came to his position as a mortal human, but became a [[Dark Angels]] [[Space Marine]] during the recruitment period that followed the Imperium's discovery of Caliban.{{Fn|8}} This Lord Cypher was rumoured to be the last surviving [[Knights of Lupus|Knight of Lupus]], who escaped his order's destruction and somehow made his way into the ranks of the Order.{{Fn|1}} However, the novel [[Angels of Caliban (Novel)|Angels of Caliban]] makes this unlikely, as it portrays this Lord Cypher as an ally of the [[Watchers in the Dark]] and an enemy of [[Chaos]], whereas the Knights of Lupus sought to preserve the Chaos-tainted Great Beasts of Caliban and books from their library contributed to Luther's fall to Chaos. Furthermore, [[Zahariel]] recognized this Lord Cypher after removing his helm, which would be improbable if he was a former Knight of Lupus.{{Fn|7}}
*[[Zahariel El'Zurias]], who ordered the former Lord Cypher's death after he attempted to kill him during a coup and was promoted to his place by Luther.{{Fn|7}} It is not known if Zahariel is the Lord Cypher that is active in the fortieth millennium, but this would go some way towards explaining his enigmatic behavior and allegiances, as Zahariel was a powerful Chaos sorcerer who joined a rebellion against the Imperium but was not aligned with [[Horus]] or the other traitor legions. Furthermore, the current Lord Cypher is said to be one of the Fallen, which Zahariel was. During his most recent capture by the Dark Angels, Cypher spoke a codeword "Starfire", the codeword which had been used to activate the orbital defense weapons against Lion El'Jonson's fleet, which was originally known by only four people: [[Luther]], [[Astelan]], [[Griffayn]], & Zahariel.{{Fn|6a}}{{Fn|12}}

During the beginning of the [[Horus Heresy]], Cypher would assist in a prison-break and extraction of [[Garviel Loken]], a member of the [[Knights-Errant]] who was sent to [[Caliban]] by [[Malcador the Sigilite]] to determine the allegiance of [[Luther]]. Working with [[Iacton Qruze]], a old friend from the time of the [[Great Crusade]], Cypher managed to exfiltrate both from the dungeon, but ultimately refused their offer to join them as one of Malcador's agents. Instead he would serve in the shadows, loyal but unremembered.{{Fn|15}}

At the end of the Heresy, [[Lion El'Jonson]] returned to Caliban to find Luther turned to the forces of [[Chaos]]. El'Jonson landed and took up the fight against Luther while the [[Dark Angels]] fleet bombarded the planet from above. When Luther defeated El'Jonson, he realised his mistakes and collapsed, unwilling to fight any more. The Chaos Gods realised their chosen had failed and sent a vast [[Warp Storm]] to suck up the traitor Dark Angels and spread them across time and space.{{citethis}}

===Post-Heresy===
The Lord Cypher, or perhaps someone impersonating him, was one of these Fallen Angels, but no one actually knows his true name. Two members of [[The Order]], [[Sar Daviel]] and Master [[Remial]], claimed that he was a survivor of the Knights of Lupus and joined [[The Order]] under a false name after [[Lion El'Jonson]] destroyed them{{Fn|1}}.
[[Image:CypherFight.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Cypher battles Dark Angels{{Fn|5}}]]
Cypher is believed to have first been identified acting an enemy of the Dark Angels during the [[Forgotten Wars]].{{Fn|5}} Since then, he appears randomly throughout the galaxy, but is rumoured to be slowly moving towards [[Terra]]. He is famous for his pistol abilities, being able to fire precisely with every shot, even when using two weapons, no matter the chaos of the battle around him. His characteristic combination of [[Bolt Pistol]] and [[Plasma Pistol]] are known throughout the [[galaxy]] as rumours fill every [[Segmentum]] of the presence of a white-robed man in power armour.{{citethis}}

Cypher may be attempting to rewrite the history of the Dark Angels and Fallen. In [[M41]] he turned himself in to the [[Inner Circle]] and with the help of the [[Watchers in the Dark]] managed to convince them to use [[Tuchulcha]] and its brother engines to open up a time rift over the ruins of Caliban ostensibly to prevent [[Astelan]] and [[Typhus]] from doing the same. The rift was [[Battle of the Caliban System|ultimately destroyed]] by [[Azrael]], creating the same warp storm that originally scattered the Fallen. After the battle, Cypher vanishes.{{Fn|6}}

====Terran Crusade====
Cypher again reappeared during the [[Terran Crusade]], this time with the [[Harlequin]] [[Sylandri Veilwalker]]. While aboard a [[Red Corsairs]] [[Blackstone Fortress]], Cypher and Sylandri killed the Corsair guarding [[Roboute Guilliman]] and his [[Ultramarines]]. After taking the key he talked to Guilliman, and told him he would free him if he brought Cypher to [[Terra]] and the [[Golden Throne]]. Guilliman agreed, so Cypher freed him and the Ultramarines.{{Fn|9a}} Cypher and Sylandri then helped them free the rest of their allies and then guided them to the Harlequin's [[Webway Portal]].{{Fn|9b}} Once in the [[webway]], Cypher was met by some of his [[Fallen]] allies.{{Fn|9c}} Cypher accompanied Guilliman on the rest of the journey to Terra, and fought in the battle against [[Magnus]] on [[Luna]].{{Fn|9d}} Once Guilliman and the members of the crusade arrived outside the main chamber of the Golden Throne, he broke the deal he made with Cypher and ordered the [[Adeptus Custodes]] to arrest Cypher and his [[Fallen]] allies. This caused Cypher to snarl in anger, and he unholstered his weapons briefly before he and his allies surrendered. They were then taken to a warded prison block.{{Fn|9e}}

====Escape from the Dark Cells====
{{Spoiler|source=Cypher: Lord of the Fallen (Novel)}}''
Cypher and the Fallen with him (including [[Azkhar]], [[Bakhariel]], [[Korlael]]) were able to escape their confinement in the [[Dark Cells]] after a small Dark Angel force led by [[Mordachi]], which had snuck and murdered their way into the palace seeking the Fallen for themselves, destroyed the generators to the dark cells. While normally the dark cells has many redundancies, the [[Battle of Lion's Gate|war on Terra]], warp incursion, and other damages caused the actions of the Dark Angels to have cascading effects freeing those in the dark cells.{{Fn|14a}} Avoiding the hunting Dark Angels, Custodes, and [[Officio Assassinorum|Imperial Assassins]]{{Fn|14b}}, Cypher and his Fallen brethren were able to retrieve their wargear and cause mass confusion through destroying the central palace communication hub, allowing them to slip past their many pursuers and enter the maze of Catacombs beneath the Imperial Palace. Cypher then revealed he intended to not flee Terra but instead reach the [[Imperial Dungeon|Throneroom]].{{Fn|14c}} Using a forgotten doorway to the [[Sanctum Imperialis]] dubbed the Path of Martyrs, Cypher and his group were able to fight off the pursuing Dark Angels and Assassins.{{Fn|14d}} Cypher was about to reach the Throneroom through the [[Bridge of Ascension]] when he was confronted by the badly wounded [[Custodian Warden]] [[ Hekkarron]], who guided by a vision of the Emperor Himself told the Lord of the Fallen “not yet”. Cypher accepted the message and left the Palace thereafter.{{Fn|14e}}

Having escaped, Cypher is once again pursued by the Dark Angels, leading them to devastation at the [[Massacre at Darkmor]].{{Fn|10}} His original jailers are also in pursuit in the form of a combined [[Adeptus Custodes]] and [[Sisters of Silence]] force under the [[Shield-Captain]] [[Daryth]].{{Fn|11}}

====Other Notable Actions====
*Involvement in the [[Forgotten Wars]] (First Contact).{{Fn|5}}
*Instigating the [[Septius VII Uprising]]{{Fn|5}}
*Killing the [[Ork]] [[Warboss]] who killed [[Dark Angels Supreme Grand Master]] [[Alloken]] during the [[Red Stars Campaign]]. His intervention prevents the Master's artifacts from being stolen by Greenskins.{{Fn|5}}
*Nearly destroying the Dark Angels after they attempted to parlay with him during the time of [[Supreme Grand Master]] [[Morderan]]{{Fn|12a}}.
*Potentially acting as the [[Saviour of Praxus]] during the [[Nova Terra Interregnum]].{{Fn|5}}
*Raiding the world of [[Voss Prime]] with the [[Black Legion]] to steal [[STC]] documents{{Fn|5}}
*Aiding the [[Silver Skulls]] against the [[Cult of the Red Heresy]] in the [[Plague of Unbelief]]{{Fn|5}}
*Saving [[Cadian]] soldiers on [[Monarch Prime]] and leading them against [[Cultist]]s.{{Fn|5}}
*Becoming leader of the [[Zargosoan Smuggler Fleet]] and attacking the [[Black Gulf Mines]], which it turns out may have been one of [[The Fallen]].{{Fn|5}}
*Replacing [[Inquisitor]] [[Arnuldus]] to instigate the collapse of the [[Hive World]] of [[Septius VII]]{{citethis}}
*Involvement in the [[Hundred Planet Rebellion]]{{citethis}}
*Cypher was present at the final battle of the liberation of Amadis, rallying the overwhelmed defenders in the face of Chaos cultist artillery and human wave assaults. Regan Antigone, the only trooper of the Procell 1st Irregulars who survived, swore an oath to Cypher not to reveal his presence, taking the credit for Cypher's actions. Decades later, 6th Company Master Tigrane learned the truth from now-Colonel Antigone at a social function. Master Tigrane declared Colonel Antigone a traitor for associating with Cypher and summarily executed him{{Fn|4}}.
*During several bloody battles during the [[Escovan Campaign]] of 989.[[M41]], the [[Red Corsairs]] vow to slay Cypher.{{Fn|5}}
*Under the guise of the [[Voice of the Emperor]], spreading the [[Plague of Unbelief_#Second Plague of Unbelief|Second Plague of Unbelief]]. All attempts by the [[Officio Assassinorum]] to kill him are failures, and he later escapes [[Black Templars]] captivity.{{Fn|5}}
*Escaping [[Belial]] on three separate occasions.{{Fn|5}}
*Killing [[Inquisitor]] [[Rasputin]] when he learned too much about the history of the [[Dark Angels]].{{Fn|5}}

==Equipment==
He wears robes over his [[Power Armour]] in an attempt to hide himself, but this look has made him obvious. Perhaps this was the point, but he does seem to attract other members of the Fallen Angels to his side. It is unknown how they communicate and why they are drawn to him.{{citethis}}

The final distinguishing feature of Cypher is his sword. It is a mysterious weapon that he has never been seen to draw on the battlefield, though rumours surround it: it is an artifacts of the Dark Angels; it is the [[Lion Sword]]; it is broken; Cypher seeks to reforge it and present it to the [[Emperor of Mankind]], obtaining absolution and forgiveness. Cypher is notable for wielding twin pistols, a [[Plasma Pistol]] and [[Bolt Pistol]].{{Fn|10}}

Cypher has been seen carrying a [[C’tan]] phase knife – a weapon similar to the [[C’tan phase sword]] used by the [[Callidus Assassin]]s. The knife was at some point lost in battle with the C’tan known as [[the Deceiver]] in the opening stages of the [[13th Black Crusade]]. However, the battle occurred in the [[Warp]] and seems to have been subject to a strange loop in either the time continuum or reality itself. Cypher is most often seen without the blade.{{Fn|5}}

