Czagra.wikitext:
{{IronWarriorsPortal}}
'''Czagra, the Grandmarshal of Ruin''' is a powerful [[Iron Warriors]] [[Warsmith]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:Czagra.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|3}}]]
He commands a vast horde of [[Chaos]] forces, with Czagra's personal [[Chaos Warband|Warband]], the [[Effacers of Medrengard]], being at the head of it. The [[Warsmith]]'s other forces include the [[Barbican Lords]] and [[Ferrocratic Creed]] [[Iron Warriors]] Warbands, who have pledged to serve him, along with the [[Riven Reforged]] [[Chaos Cult]], and [[Princeps]] from the [[Traitor Titan Legions]] [[Legio Krytos|Krytos]] and [[Legio Rorgahl]]. Czagra also has compacts with several [[Dark Mechanicum]] [[Hell Forge]]s and has a coven of [[Cybertheurge]], which include the [[Chaos Sorcerer]] [[Mekranteer]]. He usually commands these forces to utterly destroy worlds and orchestrates meticulously planned strategies from his flagship, [[Forgemaul]]. In [[M42]] Czagra was carrying out these attacks within the [[Vorlishk Sub-sector]] and was in the process of destroying [[Narrotor]], when the [[Arks of Omen Campaign]] began.{{Fn|1}}

The [[Warsmith]] would take part in the [[Arks of Omen Campaign|Campaign]] and became a commander of one of [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s [[Ark of Omen]]s, after pledging to use it to track down one of a series of artefacts known as a [[Key-Fragment]]. Each Fragment had a unique [[warp]] signature and Czagra's Ark, [[Herald of Misery]], tracked its location to the [[Shrine World]] [[Lume IV]]. With his forces consisting entirely of subservient [[Iron Warriors]] [[Chaos Warband|Warbands]], oathsworn [[Traitor Titan Legions]] and enslaved [[Chaos Cult]]s, the [[Warsmith]]'s [[Balefleet]] completely followed his commands at they attacked the world. Weeks of siege warfare ended with the Warsmith claiming the Key-Fragment he had been sent to claim and showing that Czagra's Balefleet was one of the most lethally efficient in the first wave of their creation.{{Fn|2}}

