'''Czarn the Cyberoth''' is an infamous [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromundan]] [[Heretek]] that once led the [[Brethren of the Black Dawn]] [[Chaos Cult|Techno-Heresy Cult]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
In the aftermath of the [[Great Rift]]'s creation, the [[Hive World]] was left in disarray. This led the [[Brethren of the Black Dawn]] to join the various [[Chaos]] forces, [[mutants]], and monsters that attacked the [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]] surface settlement known as [[Cinderak City]]. However, they did so just as a massive battle broke out as [[House Escher]] defended the city from the invading forces of [[House Goliath]]. Caught between the [[Clan House]]s, most of the Brethren were slain, without the two opposing forces even knowing the [[Chaos Cult|Techno-Heresy Cult]] was there. Czarn survived the battle but was left mortally wounded, and used his last moments to transfer his brain into one of the Brethren's [[Scrap-Code Ambot]]s. The operation was a success and the Heretek then used the Ambot to drink deep of a power conduit that was connected to an ancient plasma reactor beneath Cinderak City. The energy further reshaped Czarn's new form and caused [[Chaos|corrupted]] organic growths to cover the Ambot. Cultists then gathered around him, drawn by whispers of the [[Warp]], and they greeted Czarn as their new master.{{Fn|1}}

However, soon afterward Czarn and his army were attacked beneath [[Cinderak City]] by the forces of both [[House Escher]] and [[House Goliath]]. In the three-way war that followed, Czarn found himself fighting the Goliath [[Stimmer]] [[Gorshiv Hammerfist]]. Despite his new form and abilities, the [[Heretek]] was defeated by Hammerfist, who destroyed Czarn's [[Ambot]] body. However, because its destruction occurred as the Heretek was grasping a power conduit, Czarn's essence somehow survived intact. After going down ancient powerlines, the Heretek observed Hammerfist at first, before he lost interest and began searching for a new form to dwell in.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Apocrypha Necromunda: Daemons of Meridian]], pgs. 1-5

