Dagan.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
An [[Intercessor]] belonging to Ariston Squad of the [[Lamenters]], Dagan served as part of the strike force sent to drive the Tyranids from the world of Raphaela. Despite the world suffering Tyrannaforming advanced enough that even the enhanced physiology of the Astartes could find the atmosphere potentially lethal, it was considered vital by Imperial logicians, due to being the sector's breadbasket.{{Fn|1a}} Lamenters of Repentant Company{{Fn|1b}} and the Third Penitential Company,{{Fn|1c}} of which Dagan was a part, were deployed to the city of Pallas on Raphaela's southern continent,{{Fn|1d}} alongside the [[White Panthers]], [[Blood Angels]], and elements of the [[Astra Militarum]].{{Fn|1e}}

The strike force suffered heavy losses. Dagan's squad was overwhelmed while providing support for a [[Predator]] tank, which was subsequently destroyed. Dagan suffered a mortal wound as xenos talons stabbed through his abdomen, but it was not immediately lethal.{{Fn|1f}} 

He was dug out of the pile of corpses by the [[Eliminator]] [[Ramethos]]. Upon learning the fellow Lamenter had sworn to slay the [[Tyranid Prime]] leading this swarm, Dagan requested to join him in his [[Oath of Moment]]. Arming himself with a supply of [[Krak grenade]]s and as much ammunition as he could carry, Dagan sacrificed himself by providing a diversion upon the steps of an Imperial temple. This drew away the [[Gargoyles]] protecting the Prime, allowing the Eliminator to kill the leader beast with his final Executioner round.{{Fn|1}}

Although Ramethos could see Lamenter [[Thunderhawks]] beginning to seek out survivors, Dagan succumbed to his wounds before he could be rescued.{{Fn|1g}}


