Daleth Tencin.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
'''Daleth Tencin''' was a [[Magos Biologis]] and [[Xenologist]], who was obsessed with the physical manifestation of [[Warp]] [[Daemons|entities]]. She later complied her research on the subject and wrote the [[Historia Empyrealium]] [[Xenology (Imperium)|Xenology]] text.{{Fn|1}} 

Born on the [[Forge World]] [[Kappa Prime]], she led several [[Explorator Fleet]]s across [[Segmentum Obscuras]] for her research on [[Daemons|entities]]. Tencin was such a driven individual, and so respected by her fellow [[Tech-Priest]]s, that she was able to travel to areas that were dangerously close to the [[Eye of Terror]]. When Tencin pushed further and finally reached the regions around the Eye, however, she was confronted by the [[Ordo Hereticus]]. The Ordo had become aware of her research and ordered her to cease her work and return to Kappa Prime at once. When Tencin refused to do so, several squadrons of [[Space Marines]] from the [[Relictors]] [[Chapter]] were sent to "persuade her" to comply with the Ordo's orders. It is unclear as to what happen next, but Tencin vanished after the squadrons boarded her flagship, [[Duodecim]]. The Ordo Heretictus and Relictors would make no comment on the matter, leading Tencin to be presumed deceased. The Duodecim was also declared to be lost and the name Daleth Tencin drifted from history.{{Fn|1}} 

Nearly 3 centuries later, though, Tencin's name was heard again, on the [[Hive World]] [[Orrotha]]. It lay to the galactic south of the [[Eye of Terror]] and was suffering from an insurrection, when a [[Relictors]] strike force arrived to restore order. As they began to do so, though, a colossal [[Warp]] emanation, resembling a arachnid, destroyed several of their squads and forced them to abandon their positions around Orrotha's capital. The insurrections the Warp emanation like a god and referred to it as '''Daleth the Tencin'''. Tencin's supporters have long argued that the similar names are just a coincidence and the Warp emanation has nothing to do with her. However, Daleth the Tencin has gone on to be recorded as appearing several times since Orrotha's insurrection and each time, it has attacked the Relictors' forces.{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Liber Xenologis]], pg. 138 - A Brief History of Xenology 
