Dalin Larsekson.wikitext:
{|align="right"
|align="right"|{{NecromundaPortal}}
|-
|align="right"|{{SquatPortal}}
|}
'''Dalin Larsekson, the Mad Mechanic of Red Ruin,''' is a [[Charter Master]] of the [[Ironhead Squat Prospector]] [[Jardlan]] clan on [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
He once resided within [[Jardlan]]'s [[Stronghold|Holdfast]], but was asked to leave when his engineering projects began to routinely damage it. Taking his work and followers with him, Larsekson came to occupy his clan's remote outpost in the [[Red Ruin]] mountain. It was while he was there, that the [[Charter Master]] met the [[Squat]] [[Bounty Hunter]] [[Grendl Grendlsen]], who told him of the treasures located on a spaceship within [[Hive Primus]]' [[Sump]] settlement, [[Heretic's Hole]]. Most importantly among them, Grendlsen suspected, was an [[Ancestral Shard]] of the ancient [[Squat Mining Charter]]s. Upon hearing this, Larsekson sought to claim it and convinced a group of his followers to aid him in doing so.{{Fn|1}}  

With [[Herga]] serving as his second-in-command, the [[Charter Master]] led his group aboard a number of [[Dust Crawler]]s to [[Hive Primus]]. Once there, they would travel to the [[Hive]]'s Sump and attempt to infiltrate the Heretic's Hole's spaceship. However Larsekson's group was spotted by its ruler [[Ursan Graves]], who led a number of his forces to confront them. Graves was a powerful [[Wyrd (Psyker)|Wyrd]] who had turned Heretic's Hole into a sanctuary for his kind and feared the invaders were agents of [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]]'s [[Imperial Commander]] [[Gerontius Helmawr]]. This led Graves to warn Larsekson to leave his settlement, but the Charter Master refused and a fight broke out between the two forces. Though it ended with the Charter Master's group retreating, Larsekson would not relent in his quest for the [[Ancestral Shard]].{{Fn|1}}  

They would try again and succeed in cutting their way into spaceship, due to [[Herga]]'s use of a [[Vartijan Exo-Driller]]. The [[Charter Master]] and [[Ursan Graves|Graves]]' forces would clash once more, but during the battle Larsekson found and fled with the Ancestral Shard. His surviving followers joined him, though many had died; including Herga who gave her life, so Larsekson could escape. While his quest was now over, Larsekson was far from home and his adventures in [[Hive Primus]]' [[Underhive]] were just beginning...{{Fn|1}}   

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Apocrypha Necromunda: The Lost Charter]], pgs. 1-4

