Damos.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
'''Brother Damos''' is a [[Dreadnought]] of the [[Angels Porphyr]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Damos was the commander of the Chapter's [[9th Company (Angels Porphyr)|9th Company]]. He was well respected as a [[Veteran Space Marine|veteran]] of three centuries of service to the chapter; under his command the 9th was considered a model of the [[Devastator]] doctrine.{{Fn|1}}

During the scouring of [[Hume]], a surprise air attack on his position at '''Hill 236''' caught Brother Damos out in the open as he moved about the position's bunkers. The rebel [[Marauder Bombers]] smashed the position for hours. Damos' body was recovered but was declared shattered beyond the skill of the [[Apothecary|Apothecaries]] to repair. He demanded the right to fight on, so his body was placed in [[stasis]] and transferred to the [[Fortress monastery|Chapter's Monastery]] where it was laid to rest in the armoured sarcophagus of a [[Dreadnought]]. Brother Damos has since given three millennia of service to the chapter.{{Fn|1}}

