Danial Tan Draconis.wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Knight]] of [[House Draconis]], and the son and heir to its [[High King]] [[Tolwyn Tan Draconis]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Draconis was heir when the [[Word Bearers]] [[Betrayal on Donatos|invaded]] the [[Imperium]] [[Industrial World]] [[Donatos]]. High King Tolwyn later led [[Adrastapol]]'s [[Knight House]]s to aid in Donatos' defense, but disaster struck during the battle, when the Adrastapol Knight Houses, [[House Chimaeros|Chimaeros]] and [[House Wyvorn|Wyvorn]] began attacking their fellow Knights. Their Thrones Mechanicums had been tainted through [[Chaos]] witchery and in the bloody betrayal that followed, High King Tolwyn was killed and it fell to Danial, to rally together the remnants of Houses [[House Draconis|Draconis]], [[House Pegasson|Pegasson]] and [[House Minotos|Minotos]]' forces. He then united his Knights with the other scattered Imperial forces defending Donatos and launched a determined attack, that sought vengeance upon both the traitorous Houses and the Word Bearers.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Imperial Knights (8th Edition)]], pg. 53 — ''A Tapestry of Glories: Betrayal on Donatos''

