Danidel.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
'''Danidel''' is a [[Fallen Angel]], who wields an ancient [[Heavy bolter#Sol Militaris Pattern|Sol Militaris-pattern]] [[heavy bolter]]. He is among those that now loyally serve their returned [[Primarch]] [[Lion El'Jonson]]{{Fn|1b}}, as the [[Risen (The Fallen)|Risen]].{{Fn|1c}}
==History==
After he emerged into [[Realspace]], millennia after [[Destruction of Caliban|Caliban's destruction]], Danidel eventually joined [[Echo Station]]'s [[Fallen Angels]]{{Fn|1b}}, who were led by the Fallen [[Guain]]. The [[Space Station]] would have dealings with the [[pirate]] fleet led by the Fallen [[Borz (Fallen Angel)|Borz]], but this would not stop the pirate leader from stealing Echo Station's supplies in order to repair his fleet. Shortly after the theft, though, Borz returned and Guain had the Space Station's weapons lock on to the pirate fleet. By then, however, Borz had pledged to serve the [[Dark Angels]]' returned [[Primarch]] [[Lion El'Jonson]], who requested that the Fallen aid him in defending the embattled [[Imperium]]. This in turn caused Borz to tell the Primarch of Echo Station, and El'Jonson had wished to meet with Guain's Fallen Angels{{Fn|1a}} 

Upon learning of this, [[Guain]] agreed to meet with [[El'Jonson]], but he still felt anger towards the [[Primarch]], for starting the [[Dark Angel]]'s civil war, that [[Destruction of Caliban|destroyed]] [[Caliban]]. This was shared by many of the [[Space Station]]'s Fallen, but it was also mixed with weariness, that the Primarch sought to kill them for their actions in the war. However El'Jonson would refute this upon his arrival at [[Echo Station|Echo]] and claimed he had no wish to reopen the wounds of the past by placing blame for what occurred. The Primarch then asked for their help in saving the embattled [[Imperium]], but if they refused, he would simply leave and not bother them again. Guain's Fallen would then voice their their long-held grievances towards their Primarch and question why they would save the decrepit Imperium, that had regressed so far from what it once was. El'Jonson simply explained that the faultless people of the Imperium, still deserved to be defended and not left to be preyed upon by [[Humanity]]'s enemies.{{Fn|1a}} 

The [[Fallen Angel]] [[Lamor]] then asked what foe was the [[Primarch]] currently fighting and [[El'Jonson]] replied that it was the [[Ten Thousand Eyes]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. Upon hearing that they faced the forces of the corrupted Fallen [[Seraphax]], Lamor immediately agreed to fight by the Primarch's side{{Fn|1a}}. Danidel and the rest of [[Echo Station]]'s Fallen agreed to do the same shortly afterwards.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
*1: [[The Lion: Son of the Forest (Novel)]]
**{{Endn|1a}}: Chapter 25
**{{Endn|1b}}: Chapter 27
**{{Endn|1c}}: Chapter 32 

