'''Darius''' was a member of the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter]], who served in the [[Deathwatch]]'s [[Kill Team Primus]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Space Marine II}}
They were among the [[Imperial]] forces that defended{{Fn|1b}} the [[Recidious System]], after it was invaded by a [[Leviathan]] [[Splinter Fleet]].{{Fn|1c}} Kill Team Primus later answered{{Fn|1b}} [[Archmagos]] [[Nozick Beta-12]]'s plea for aid on [[Kadaku]], after the [[Xenos]] threatened the secretive [[Project Aurora]], that Nozick was developing. Because of the Archmagos' call for restrain in defending Kadaku, in order to prevent damaging the Project's facility,{{Fn|1a}} [[Kill Team Primus]] was charged with deploying a [[Virus Bomb]] to kill the [[Tyranids]].{{Fn|1b}} 

However the [[Kill-Team]]'s [[Corvus Blackstar]] was attacked by a swarm of [[Gargoyle]]s, as they neared the '''Orbital Launcher Facility''' that would be used to launch the [[Virus Bomb]]. In the battle that followed, the [[Black Templar]] [[Beren]] was able to hold onto the bomb, as most of [[Kill Team Primus]] was thrown from the gunship before it crashed. While he was able to remain with the gunship, though, the others were scattered in the area around the Facility. Though Darius survived the crash, he was attacked by the [[Tyranids]] soon afterwards. Without the aid of his fellow Primus members, the [[Dark Angel]] was eventually overwhelmed and killed by the [[Xenos]]. He was later found by the Kill-Team's leader, the [[Deathwatch Black Shield|Black Shield]] [[Demetrian Titus]], who recovered Darius' [[Bolt Pistol]]. As he armed himself with it, Titus swore that he would make the weapon roar in the Dark Angel's name. The Black Shield soon became the only member of Kill Team Primus that still lived, but he was able to successfully complete their mission.{{Fn|1b}} 
