Davian Thule.wikitext:
{{BloodRavensPortal}}
[[Image:Thule.jpg|150px|thumb|right|[[Blood Ravens]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Davian Thule{{Fn|2}}]]

[[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] '''Davian Thule''' is a long-serving officer of the [[Blood Ravens]].{{Fn|1}}<sup>,</sup>{{Fn|2}}

==Biography==
===Morga===
[[Image:Thule.JPG|200px|thumb|right|[[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Davian Thule{{Fn|1}}]]
When the [[Chaos]] witch [[Morga]] seduced the [[Planetary Governor]] of a once-prosperous and loyal [[Imperium|Imperial]] colony, the [[Blood Ravens]] retaliated, purging the world of all life. Morga however, survived. She proved to be a deadly foe and slew the Blood Ravens expedition leader and most of his staff. It was the young Blood Ravens [[Neophyte|Initiate]] Davian Thule who ultimately killed her, proving his mettle early on.{{Fn|1a}}

===Cadia===
Thule led the [[Blood Ravens]] [[4th Company (Blood Ravens)|4th Company]] on [[Cadia]]. There, his men dropped on the [[Iron Warriors]] who were marching towards the city of [[Kasr Sonnen]]. The battle initially went in favour of the Blood Ravens, but word came that the [[Black Legion]] was en route as well, and orders came down from the Blood Ravens' [[Chapter Master]] to withdraw. [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Thule resisted the order and pressed his advantage until the Chapter Master threatened to have him removed from command. Thule and the Blood Ravens then left, leaving the [[Cadian]] [[Regiment]]s to fend for themselves against the Black Legion.{{Fn|2}}

===Kronus===
[[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Thule commanded the three [[Blood Ravens]] [[Space Marine Company|companies]] deployed to [[Kronus]] to purge the [[Necron]] presence there. He ordered to [[Governor-Militant]], [[Lukas Alexander]], to evacuate all civilians and [[Imperial Guard]] personnel, but Alexander refused, which forced the Blood Ravens to fight the [[Imperium|Imperial]] soldiers to achieve their objective. Thule regretted having to kill his fellow brothers-in-arms, but orders were orders.{{Fn|1b}}

Thule treated the remnants of the shattered [[1st Kronus Regiment]] with honour, arranging transport off-planet for the surviving Guardsmen, and giving [[Lukas Alexander|Alexander]]'s body a formal military burial. On the other hand, the soldiers of the rebellious [[5th Company (1st Kronus)|5th company]], who had mutinied against the [[Regiment]] and fought with the [[Blood Ravens]] during the final battle at [[Victory Bay]], were executed for disloyalty.{{Fn|1b}} Nevertheless, the survivors of the regiment bore a deep hatred for the Blood Ravens.{{Cite This}}

Thule and the [[Blood Ravens]] [[2nd Company (Blood Ravens)|Second Company]] also succeeded in their mission to wipe out the [[Necron]]s of [[Kronus]], with Thule personally planting the bomb deep within their catacombs beneath [[Thur'Abis Plateau]]. The Second Company later adopted the motto ''"Victory Over Death"'' in reference to this great victory.{{Fn|1c}}

Thule himself suffered grievous wounds in the final battle with the [[Necron Lord]], including the loss of his right eye. Nevertheless, he survived and led the [[Blood Ravens]] to victory. His lost eye was later replaced by a [[augmetic]] one.{{Fn|2}}

In the aftermath of the [[Kronus Campaign]], the [[Inquisition]] arrived to question the [[Blood Ravens]]' actions, but the commanding officers managed to finagle their way through the interrogations by claiming they were just "following orders" from their [[Chapter Master]].{{Fn|1d}}

=== Aurelian Crusades ===
[[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Thule was made commander of [[Space Marine]] operations in [[Subsector Aurelia]] and charged with protecting the [[Blood Ravens]]' recruiting worlds of [[Calderis]], [[Typhon Primaris]], and [[Meridian]]. Thule's men were at the forefront of the fighting on Calderis when the [[Tyranid]] swarm initially made planetfall. Holding the line at the cost of many of his men, Davian Thule was mortally wounded in the attack. While an [[Space Marine|Astartes]] would normally be able to recover from the types of wounds he sustained, a highly volatile Tyranid poison was ravaging his body, which forced the fleet's [[Apothecarion]] to put Thule into [[stasis]]. [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Aramus]], assuming command as [[Force Commander]], was tasked with recovering samples from Tyranid organisms across the subsector to help create an antidote to the poison.{{Fn|2}}

[[Image:Thule Dreadnought.jpg|150px|thumb|right|Davian Thule in his [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] body{{Fn|2}}]]

With these samples, [[Apothecary]] [[Gordian]] and [[Techmarine]] [[Martellus]] were able to revive [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] Thule inside a [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] chassis. For a short time, Thule's perception was hazy and he had trouble communicating with his fellow Blood Ravens, even mistaking Sergeant [[Thaddeus (Blood Ravens)|Thaddeus]] for [[Gabriel Angelos]]. Eventually, Thule's memory cleared and he once more became an invaluable part of the [[Blood Ravens]] defending the sector.{{Fn|2}}

[[Cyrus]] later revealed that Thule had found and read records of the [[Blood Ravens]]' origins during the [[Kronus Campaign]], but destroyed them. While it is likely that the documents did not reveal the corruption in the [[Chapter]]'s ranks, the revelation that the Blood Ravens have possibly descended from a [[traitor]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] could have potentially torn the Chapter apart.{{Fn|2}}

==Conflicting Sources==
{{Trivia}}
[[Dawn of War III]] confirms that Gabriel Angelos survived the [[Aurelian Crusade]], and this most reflects the [[Blood Raven]] campaign narrative, following the actions of then [[Captain]] [[Apollo Diomedes]]. Thule is not present or mentioned in the Blood Raven campaign missions.{{Fn|5}}

Per the Chaos Campaign missions, it is possible Thule may have been killed or at the very least had his [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] armour critically damaged by [[Eliphas]] on [[Typhon]]. In those missions, the two meet combat shortly before the [[Ordo Malleus]] arrived in the sector to begin [[Exterminatus]]. Weighed against this is the fact that the campaign missions are largely identical in terms of locations and narrative context (as though they are meant for one campaign to have taken place rather than all of them at once, for example it is logical to conclude only one such group would slay [[Azariah Kyras]] on [[Cyrene]]), and indeed, Eliphas is slain in the Blood Raven mission which takes place in what appears to be the exact same location on Typhon.{{Fn|3}}

==Wargear==
On [[Kronus]], Thule was armed with a standard-issue [[Chainsword]] and [[Bolt Pistol]], which he was later able to swap for a [[Daemonhammer]] and [[Meltagun]], or the [[Power sword]] [[Alexian's Blade]].{{Fn|1b}}

Before his conversion into a [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]], he wielded a [[Heavy bolter]] and wore a [[master-crafted]] [[Power armour]].{{Fn|2}}

He also carried the [[Power sword]] ''"[[Wisdom]]"'', which later passed on to [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Aramus]].{{Fn|4}}

