Davos Lamertine.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source=Void King (Novel)}}
'''Davos Lamertine''' was the head of the [[Rogue Trader House]] [[House Lamertine|Lamertine]] and the '''Void King''' of the [[Davamir Compact]], an alliance of [[Rogue Trader]]s.{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
He had hoped to pass both titles to his daughter and chosen heir [[Evelyne Lamertine|Evelyne]]{{Fn|1a}}, but she was lost in a [[Warp Storm]] before that could occur.{{Fn|1f}} Afterwards, Davos was forced to name his son [[Erastus Lamertine|Erastus]] as heir in her place, much to Davos' frustration. Davos believed that Erastus had spent his years slinking around the corners of his family and had tarnished his honour attempting to advance his standing. Because of this, Davos did not believe his son was ready to become the Void King and lead the Rogue Trader Houses that serve it. For while the Houses normally follow the King's command, they each vie for the position as well and seek to claim it for themselves. Worse still, Davos' grip on his title was not as strong as it once was. When he called for a meeting aboard the Compact's base of operations, the [[Cradle (Space Station)|Cradle]], there were some Rogue Trader Houses that refused to attend.{{Fn|1a}}

In early [[M42]], Davos received an edict from the reborn [[primarch]] [[Roboute Guilliman]], ordering the Compact to muster and attempt to find a stable route through the [[Great Rift]] into the [[Imperium Nihilus]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}} However, shortly after he announced the edict to the other members of the Compact, Davos was murdered in his private study.{{Fn|1d}} As such, rulership of House Lamertine and the Compact passed to Erastus.{{Fn|1e}}

