Delayni.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
[[Lord Militant]] '''Delayni''' was a general officer of [[Warmaster]] [[Slaydo]]'s [[Crusade]] force during the early years of the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}

After the initial success of [[Operation Redrake]], several of the fleeing [[Chaos]] forces re-grouped into opportunistic raiding parties, several of which struck vulnerable supply depots and shipping lanes behind the line of the [[Imperial]] advance.  Slaydo was so irked by these forces that he tasked General Delayni with hunting them down.{{Fn|1a}}

Somewhat unusually for an [[Imperial Guard]] officer, Delayni was receptive to the advice of the [[Imperial Navy|Navy]] officers assigned to his task force, which led to several successes, including annihilating raider squadrons off [[Long Halent]] in 757.[[M41]], [[Gotthrone]] in 758, and [[Venady]] and [[Urus]] in 760, the last of which destroyed the notorious warlord [[Pater]] [[Burbethol]].{{Fn|1a}}

During the [[Battle of Balhaut]], Delayni was the next senior officer in line to take command at [[Balopolis]] after [[General]] [[Curell]] was incapacitated and his two immediate successors, [[Marshal_(Imperial_Guard)|Marshal]] [[Bernz]] and [[General]] [[Korshen]] were both killed, but could not reach the theatre in time, which allowed Curell's deputy, Commander [[Macaroth]], to take command.{{Fn|1b}}

