Delvetar Astraneus.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
The '''Arch-Lecter Delvetar Astraneus''', is the commander of the [[Rogue Trader House]] [[House Astraneus|Astraneus]], which serves as part of the [[Davamir Compact]] alliance.{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
Like the other members of their [[House Astraneus|House]], Delvetar was born in the void and as a result they are lank and pale. House Astraneus also worships in the [[Church of the Shrouded Emperor]] [[Imperial Cult]], which sees the [[Emperor]] as a being in the dark of the void as much as the light of the stars{{Fn|1b}}. Because of this faith, however, none of the other [[Davamir Compact|Compact]] Houses trust the Astraneus.{{Fn|1a}}

Delvetar initially is an enemy of [[Erastus Lamertine]] in their power struggles and is even accused of murdering [[Davos Lamertine]] by the new lord of the Compact. After an attempt to oust Erastus from power proves unsuccessful, he and his forces are banished.{{Fn|1c}}

Despite their banishment, Delvetar and his forces reappear to later aid the Compact against traitorous [[Genestealer Cult]] forces of [[House Radrexxus]], having received Erastus' earlier plea to return to provide aid.{{Fn|1d}}

==Trivia==
''Delvetar'' is referred to as they and their, in the [[Void King (Novel)]].{{Fn|1b}}

