Commander '''Demetrius''' was a [[Chaos Dreadnought]] of the [[Violators]] [[Renegade Chapter]].

==Biography==
He had been horribly wounded but his tactician's mind was intact so the Violators had him entombed in a Dreadnought shell.{{Fn|1b}} He had once been terrified of being entombed and being unable to feel the sensations that gave him reason to kill and with to worship [[Slaanesh]]. But over time his nervous system grew into the fabric of the Dreadnought and made him more sensitive than he had ever been as a full Space Marine.{{Fn|1d}} His driving desire was to absorb every sensation and everything that war had to offer.{{Fn|1c}}

He carried an [[Assault Cannon]] on his left arm and barbed energy-lashes on his right. Over one side of his chest was the Violators chapter symbol wrought in gold of a lightening bolt crossed by a dagger. On the other side was dense script chronicling the hundreds of battles he had fought in along with the kill-marks of the important enemies he had slain. On his sarcophagus in the centre of his chest was a fleshy knot like an unopened flower that was pale and dead but pulsing with the machine's heart.{{Fn|1a}} There were also [[Smoke Launcher]]s on the upper surface of his carapace.{{Fn|1d}}

During the final defence of Charybdia Keep on [[Torvendis]], he lead one hundred Violator Marines against the [[Khorne]] [[Daemon Prince]] [[Ss'll Sh'Karr]] but was eventually overpowered and eaten alive by the daemon.{{Fn|1e}}

