Deven Fracoi Esterant Mudire.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Deven Fracoi Esterant Mudire'''{{Fn|2}} is a founding member of the [[Logos Historica Verita]], alongside [[Solana (Historitor)|Solana]], [[Fabian Guelphrain]] and [[Viablo]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
Deven Mudire is an arrogant aristocrat that [[Lord Commander of the Imperium|Lord Commander]] [[Roboute Guilliman]] selected to form the [[Logos Historica Verita]]. Alongside the [[Martian]] [[Solana (Historitor)|Solana]] and a third historitor named [[Thiennes]], he was among the first selected to join the new order. Thiennes however would later be removed for displeasing Guilliman and his fall from grace greatly impacted both Solana and Deven {{Cite this}}. The two would then be joined by [[Fabian Guelphrain]], a Terran [[Adept]] who was from a lower social strata. While Solana treated Fabian with kindness, Mudire treated the Adept with disdain. However, this did not interfere with Mudire's abilities as a Historitor, and the three of them were taken by Guilliman to meet with [[Magos Dominus|Archmagos Dominus]] [[Belisarius Cawl]] at the onset of the [[Indomitus Crusade]].{{Fn|1b}} 

After arriving at Cawl's [[Ark Mechanicus]], the [[Zar-Quaesitor]], they were reminded by the [[Space Marine Captain]] [[Messinius]] to take their roles as Historitors seriously. Mudire was quick to inform the Captain that they would, as the historitors remembered what happened to their former comrade [[Thiennes]]{{Fn|1c}}. Shortly afterwards, the newly-recruited Historitors witnessed Cawl's unveiling of the [[Primaris Space Marines]]{{Fn|1d}}. 
Some days later, the [[Indomitus Crusade]] officially began and the three Historitors were assigned to [[Lord Commander of the Imperium|Lord Commander]] [[Guilliman]]'s [[Fleet Primus]], as it prepared to leave [[Terra]]. There, they were joined by a fourth historitor, [[Theodore Viablo]]. The four would be given tasks to ascertain their talent by compiling historical facts in order to establish a true history of the [[Imperium]]. If found to be of sufficient quality, their works would be given to Roboute Guilliman's [[Fleetmaster]]s to read.{{Fn|1e}}  

Around 4 years into the Indomitus Crusade, Mudire would be reassigned to [[Fleet Octus]].{{Fn|3}}

