Dha'lok.wikitext:
{{SalamandersPortal}}
'''Dha'lok''' was a [[Salamanders]] [[Legionary]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
[[File:DHA'LOK.jpg|thumb|right|250px|'''Dha'lok'''{{Fn|1}}]]
He was part of a [[Tactical Support Squad]] in the 17th Line Company, most of whom were killed by the [[Alpha Legion]] during the Isstvan V [[Dropsite Massacre]]. '''Dha'lok''' was among only twenty warriors from his company to survive the massacre. He had been knocked unconscious by a blast from a [[Vindicator]] and later awoke in the bay of a Salamanders [[Storm Eagle]], just in time to help capture the [[Sons of Horus]] warship, the [[Grey Talon]]. After rescuing numerous Loyalists, the boarders were forced to flee into the [[Warp]], where they continued the fight to eliminate every Traitor on board for several weeks.{{Fn|1}} 

Eventually, the ship, renamed 'Hesiod' in honor of one of [[Hesiod (City)|Nocturne's great cities]], joined [[Shadrak Meduson]]'s fleet and became part of his vengeance-driven [[Shattered Legion]]s.{{Fn|1}} 

==Wargear==
'''Dha'lok''' continued his role in a Tactical Support Squad, favoring the phaestos pattern [[Flamer]] he had used during the battle at the [[Urgall Depression]]. He was also skilled in using [[melta]] and [[volkite]] weaponry.{{Fn|1}}

'''Dha'lok''' wore a hybrid suit of [[Mark V]] power armour. He retained the helm and pauldrons from the [[Mark III]] armour he wore at Isstvan V, indicating that his suit was a non-production variant of Mark V.{{Fn|1}} 

