Dhalgar Thraex.wikitext:
{{DarkEldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Dark Eldar]] [[Archon]].{{Fn|1}}

An [[Archon]] of the [[Kabal of the Hollow Heart]] and younger brother to its ruler, [[Dhaemira Thraex]], he was nearly killed by [[Orks]] under [[Ufthak Blackhawk]].{{Fn|1a}} However he was able to be healed by the [[Haemonculi]] of the [[Red Harvest]], returning to his sister's side to exact vengeance on the Greenskins. In truth, Dhaemira planned to lure the Orks into [[Commorragh]]'s [[Port Tavarr]] to unify the disparate factions under her leadership.{{Fn|1b}}

In the final battle against Blackhawk's Orks inside Port Tavarr's Arena of Deathly Sorrow, Dhalgar attempted to assassinate Dhaemira's ally [[Cistrial Virn]], leading to conflict with his sister. This led to him being poisoned by her [[Venom Blade]] and left for dead.{{Fn|1c}} Later out of desperation, Dhaemira gave Dhalgar an antidote and gave him over to Ufthak's Orks so they would be able to navigate out of the [[Webway]] and leave her be.{{Fn|1d}}

