Dimav.wikitext:
{{NightLordsPortal}}
'''Dimav''' was a [[Night Lords]] [[Sorcerer]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
{{Spoiler|source=Eater of Dreams (Short Story)}}
In the last years of the [[Horus Heresy|Heresy]], [[Warhammer]] [[Horus]] ordered the [[Night Lords]] to invade the world [[Malec'Nar]]. It was home to large deposits of [[Blackstone (Material)|Blackstone]], which the Warmaster wanted the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s [[Sorcerers]] to corrupt with the [[Warp]]. After Malec'Nar fell, [[Vathras Kell]] was charged with conducting a ritual that would call the Warp to the world. It would then in turn, be amplified in power by the Blackstone. Kell would be aided in this task, by Dimav and his fellow Sorcerers [[Cyfan]] and an unnamed Night Lord. They later succeeded in their task and Malec'Nar began to give off a singular song of agony, as the great [[Ruinstorm]] raged. Afterwards, they then began using the Warp energy to begin [[Possessed|possessing]] the world's surviving population. Malec'Nar's fall became known to the Imperium and, sometime before the [[Siege of Terra]] began, the [[Knights-Errant]] [[Fel Zharost]] and [[Macer Varren]] were sent to kill them. Zharost was a former [[Terran]] Night Lord, who had been cast out after fighting to prevent the [[Nostramo]]s from corrupting his [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]. For him, this confrontation was a chance to end the Sorcerers' threat and also gain closure on his painful past with the Night Lords. Once they arrived, Zharost led the attack and they successfully killed the Sorcerers. Dimav was the second to fall, after he was impaled through the throat by Varren's [[power sword]]. After Vathras Kell's death, the Warp fled from Malec'Nar's Blackstone and the world was silenced.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Eater of Dreams (Short Story)]]

