Drystann Cromm.wikitext:
{{GreyKnightsPortal}}
'''Drystann Cromm''' was the [[Grey Knights Grand Master|Grand Master]] of the [[Grey Knights]]. He was Grand Master of the [[4th Brotherhood (Grey Knights)|Fourth Brotherhood]] and '''Keeper of the Augurium.'''{{Fn|2}}

==History==
Cromm was an exemplar of psychic martial prescience within the Fourth Brotherhood, famed for being a dependable and cool-headed commander with the ability to temper the temptations given by foresight.{{Fn|3a}} In 841.[[M41]], he led four [[Grey Knights Brotherhood|Brotherhood]]s of the Grey Knights to stop an incursion by [[Tzeentch]]ian [[Daemon]]s.{{Fn|1}}.

After recieving disturbing [[Warp]] portents with regards to the [[Choral Engine]], Cromm led an expedition to [[Malakbael]] to warn [[Fleetmaster]] [[Trincus Abconcis]] and [[Inquisitor]] [[Glori Emagna]] of a likely [[Chaos]] assault. This prediction proved correct, as soon [[Angron]] himself appeared at the head of a great Chaos host. During the subsequent [[Battle of Malak]], Cromm led a last stand against Angron and his [[Bloodthirster]] bodyguards within the inner sanctum of the Choral Engine. Despite badly wounding the Primarch and nearly banishing him back to the [[Warp]], Cromm was ultimately torn in half by the Daemon Primarch's [[Chain Axe]] ''[[Spinegrinder]]''{{Fn|3b}}

==Notes==
Cromm was described as a [[Grand Master]] originally{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2}}, but in [[Arks of Omen: Angron]] was stated to be a [[Brother-Captain]].{{Fn|3a}}

