Dumah (Chaplain).wikitext:
{{FleshTearersPortal}}
[[Image:WrathOfTheLostCoverClean.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Chaplain Dumah{{Fn|1m}}]]
'''Dumah''' is a [[Chaplain]] of the [[Flesh Tearers]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
*{{Main|Battle of Cretacia}}
In [[M42]], Dumah was summoned to the [[Battle Barge]] ''[[Victus]]'', where he met with [[Chapter Master]] [[Gabriel Seth]]. Seth explained that the Flesh Tearers homeworld of [[Cretacia]] had been cut off from contact with the Chapter for 20 years, and due to their losses [[Devastation of Baal]] the Chapter was in need of new recruits and supplies. Thus Dumah, alongside [[Captain]] [[Tanthius (Primaris Captain)|Tanthius]], were assigned to gross the [[Great Rift]] and reestablish contact with Cretacia.{{Fn|1a}}

Aboard the [[Strike Cruiser]] ''[[Cretacian Justice]]'' as Tanthius commands the [[Lunar Class Cruiser]] ''[[Herald of Virtue]]'', Dumah and the rest of his group of the 4th Company arrive near the [[Corythos System]] and encounter [[Genestealer Cult]]ists on Polaris void space. The attack is led by [[Apothecary]] [[Barachiel (Primaris Apothecary)|Barachiel]], who manages to clear the Station of Genestealer Cultists. However Barachiel learns that Tanthius was killed aboard the ''Herald of Virtue'' by a [[Clamavus]].{{Fn|1a}} Dumah leads his own boarding of the ''Herald of Virtue'', encountering more Genestealers aboard the vessel, killing a [[Genestealer Magus]].{{Fn|1b}}

After the battle, Dumah reveals to Barachiel that he intends to form a new [[Death Company]] of the Flesh Tearers with the Brother [[Isaiah]], who as recently succumbed to the [[Black Rage]], at its core alongside the crazed [[Reiver]] [[Tamael]].{{Fn|1c}} As the ''Cretacian Justice'' draws closer to its homeworld, the crew begins to go mad and mutinies from infiltration by Genestealer Cultists, forcing Dumah and the rest of the Flesh Tearers to suppress it violently.{{Fn|1c}}

After finally arriving in the Corythos System, the Flesh Tearers receive no word from Cretacia and the 4th Company lands to investigate. Dumah prioritizes claiming the [[Fortress-Monastery]] and relics, while Barachiel wishes to investigate the fate of the greater system and the possibility for the cure for the Black Rage on their homeworld. [[Venerable Dreadnought]] [[Daeron]] agrees with Dumah, and they lead a dangerous expedition through Cretacia's deadly wilderness to the Fortress-Monastery as Barachiel is left aboard the ''Cretacian Justice'' to perform genetic purity tests amongst the crew to look for any further Genestealers.{{Fn|1d}} 

Dumah and the 4th eventually reach a tribal camp, finding evidence of a massacre and learn that the female children have been taken hostage by a nearby group of raiders. After rescuing the children and slaughtering the raiders, Dumah kills a monstrous beat to prove his worth to the tribal chieftain, but more importantly finds evidence of [[Chaos Space Marine]] activity on the world.{{Fn|1e}} As the 4th investigates further, they discover a [[Khornate]] Heretic Astartes that states the Blood God covets and learn that the Chaos Space Marine warband known as the [[Disciples of Rage]] under a [[Chaos Lord]] dubbed only the [[First Disciple]] has taken over the Fortress-Monastery.{{Fn|1f}}

Dumah meets back up with Barachiel and make a plan to reclaim the Fortress-Monastery. Despite initial disagreements and arguments over whether the Black Rage belongs in the Chapter or not, Barachiel agrees to follow Dumah's plan for a frontal assault supported by orbital bombardment. The Flesh Tearers are aided by the tribes of Cretacia, which are eager to expel the Chaos invaders.{{Fn|1f}} As the ''Cretacian Justice'' launches an obrital bombardment and [[Attack Craft]] are launched to destroy the Fortresses defensive guns, Dumah orders a frontal assault despite Barachiel's warning. The first assault fails and the Flesh Tearers and their allies suffer heavy losses. Faced with annihilation Dumah agrees to follow Barachiel's plan of a subterranean infiltration to disable the fortresses power generator.{{Fn|1g}}

Infiltrating through a hidden corridor used by [[Aspirant]]s, the Flesh Tearers face only token resistance and are able to quickly reach the power generator chamber. After destroying the reactor with explosive charges, the fortresses [[Void Shield]] falls and the ''Cretacian Justice'' is able to inflict massive damage on enemy defensive positions. Dumah uses the opportunity to lead a fresh frontal assault, and though the fighting is bloody the Flesh Tearers and tribals are victorious. A berserk Dumah then encounters the First Disciple, clad in the [[Terminator Armour]] of [[Nassir Amit]], and the two engage in a vicious fight as Barachiel reaches the Black Tower and discovers some still-living captive Death Company warriors.{{Fn|1h}} Dumah releases his new Death Company as Barachiel discovers the bodies of [[Aspirant]]s horrifically mutated from a secret attempt to cure the Black Rage.{{Fn|1i}}

The Death Company is eventually able to turn the tide of the battle under Dumah's command, finally breaking through into the fortress defenses as the First Disciple falls back. The Flesh Tearers discover that the Disciples of Rage are planning to open a [[Warp]] portal in the Fortress Reliquary, and they rush to stop Cretacia becoming a [[Daemon World]] as the Death Company sacrifices itself to buy time.{{Fn|1j}} In the reliquary, Dumah is able to kill the First Disciple and recover Nassit Amit's Armour while stopping the opening of the Warp Portal.{{Fn|1k}}

After the battle, Cretacia is secured but what little population there was has been decimated while the Fortress-Monastery is heavily damaged. It is discovered that Barachiel since accepted the Black Rage to the point of recieving his own vision of [[Sanguinius]] battling [[Horus]], succumbing to the curse of their Chapter in turn.{{Fn|1l}}

