Edeon.wikitext:
{{GreyKnightsPortal}}
'''Edeon''' was a [[Grey Knights Brother-Captain|Brother-Captain]] of the [[Grey Knights]], serving in the [[2nd Brotherhood (Grey Knights)|2nd Brotherhood]].{{Fn|1}}

In '''708.[[M34]]''' he led a dozen squads into the [[Veiled Region]] seeking the [[Daemonafex]].  All communication was lost, and eventually the [[Council of Titan]] declared them lost.{{Fn|1}}

However, nearly two thousand years later in '''108.[[M36]]''', word reached [[Titan]] of the lost Brother-Captain Edeon and his brothers.  Unbeknownst to the Chapter, Edeon had followed the Daemonafex and its thralls into an area of the [[Warp]] that owed its existence to the echoes of forgotten moments.  Edeon and his Grey Knights fought at the foot of the Daemon’s Fortress of Deceit, each day falling to grievous wounds only to rise again, borne up by their unwavering resolve and psychic fury.  Faced with their combined might, the Daemonafex was finally cast down, though it was to cost Edeon and his brothers their lives in the material realm.  On their return to realspace, their bodies began to atrophy at an alarming rate.  Before he died, the Brother-Captain only had time to send a coded signal to Titan, telling of the [[Brotherhood (Grey Knights)|brotherhood's]] victory.{{Fn|1}}

